,{"type":"text_delta","text":"100.0) if you want me"},{"type":"text_delta","text":" to confirm."},{"type":"completed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"opaque","provider":"anthropic","kind":"thinking","data":{"signature":"","thinking":"","type":"thinking"}},{"type":"text","text":"Rust 1.100.0 (released 12 November 2026) doesn't appear to have any headline async changes.\n\nThe [official announcement](https://blog.rust-lang.org/2026/11/12/Rust-1.100.0/) doesn't mention async, `Future`, or `await`. The main items are:\n- **Never type:** `!` is now stable and can be named anywhere. `Infallible` is now an alias for it. The never-type fallback also changes from `()` to `!` in the 2015, 2018 and 2021 editions, which can break code in rare cases.\n- **Allocator API:** the core `Allocator` trait is stable, usable with `Vec` and `Box`.\n- **`DropGuard`:** a new type, `core::mem::DropGuard`, that runs a closure when it's dropped.\n- **`conjure_zst`:** a new function, `std::mem::conjure_zst`, for creating zero-sized values in unsafe code.\n- **Cargo:** unused-dependency warnings, a reworked `build-dir` layout, and `min-publish-age` dependency cooldowns.\n\nI also opened the [detailed release notes](https://doc.rust-lang.org/stable/releases.html#version-11000-2026-11-12). The page came back as a garbled mix of bullet fragments, and the tool truncated most of it, so I can't say for sure there's nothing async-related in it.\n\nThe only items I saw that could touch async code are `Pin` changes:\n- `pin!(x)` now always gives `Pin<&mut &mut T>` when `x` is `&mut T`.\n- Some coercions on `Pin<Foo>` are now disallowed when `Foo` doesn't implement `Deref`.\n- The safety invariants of `Pin::new_unchecked` changed slightly.\n\nBecause the notes were jumbled, I can't tell whether these belong to 1.100 or to earlier releases on the same page. If you depend on manual `Pin` or `pin!` usage, check the 1.100.0 section of the notes directly.\n\nI can look at the [Rust GitHub release page](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/releases/tag/1.100.0) if you want me to confirm."}]},"stop_reason":"end_turn","usage":{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":839,"cache_read_input_tokens":11997,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8194},"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","refusal_category":null}]}
